<!DOCTYPE html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="UTF-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1.0"><title>About — Steven Jewell</title><link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/style.css"></head><body>
<%- include('partials/nav') %>
<div class="hero hero-sm"><h1>About Steven Jewell</h1><p>ED Charge Nurse. Educator. Level I Trauma Center.</p></div>
<section class="section section-white">
  <div class="container" style="max-width:900px;">
    <div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 2fr;gap:3rem;align-items:start;">
      <div style="background:linear-gradient(135deg,var(--blue),var(--accent));border-radius:var(--radius);height:350px;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;color:white;font-size:4rem;">🏥</div>
      <div>
        <h2 style="margin-bottom:1rem;">Meet Steven</h2>
        <p style="line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:1rem;">Steven Jewell is an Emergency Department Charge Nurse at a <strong>Level I Trauma Center in San Antonio, Texas</strong>. With credentials including BSN, RN, CEN, and CPEN, he brings frontline expertise to every class he teaches.</p>
        <p style="line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:1rem;">Delivering <strong>over 250 hours of education annually</strong> to nurses and physicians across the globe, Steven bridges the gap between textbook knowledge and real-world emergency practice. His courses are built from the trenches — informed by the cases, protocols, and split-second decisions that define Level I trauma care.</p>
        <p style="line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:1rem;">From advanced trauma assessment to pediatric emergencies, from ECG interpretation to nursing leadership — Steven's teaching philosophy is simple: <em>if it doesn't help you at the bedside, it doesn't belong in the classroom.</em></p>
        <div style="margin-top:1.5rem;display:flex;gap:.8rem;flex-wrap:wrap;">
          <span class="badge badge-ce" style="font-size:.85rem;padding:.4rem .8rem;">BSN</span>
          <span class="badge badge-ce" style="font-size:.85rem;padding:.4rem .8rem;">RN</span>
          <span class="badge badge-ce" style="font-size:.85rem;padding:.4rem .8rem;">CEN</span>
          <span class="badge badge-ce" style="font-size:.85rem;padding:.4rem .8rem;">CPEN</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section section-warm">
  <div class="container">
    <h2 class="section-title">Why Learn With Steven?</h2>
    <div class="card-grid" style="margin-top:2rem;">
      <div class="card" style="padding:2rem;text-align:center;">
        <div style="font-size:2.5rem;margin-bottom:.8rem;">🔬</div>
        <h3>Evidence-Based</h3>
        <p>Every course is grounded in current research, guidelines, and best practices from leading trauma and emergency medicine organizations.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card" style="padding:2rem;text-align:center;">
        <div style="font-size:2.5rem;margin-bottom:.8rem;">🏥</div>
        <h3>Frontline Experience</h3>
        <p>Steven isn't just teaching theory — he's applying these skills every shift in one of the busiest trauma centers in the country.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card" style="padding:2rem;text-align:center;">
        <div style="font-size:2.5rem;margin-bottom:.8rem;">📜</div>
        <h3>CE Credits</h3>
        <p>Most courses qualify for Continuing Education credits. Stay current with your licensure while building real clinical confidence.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
<%- include('partials/footer') %>
</body></html>
